<div class=3D"ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message skipProofing">IETF has =
SEAT working group. It works on TLS 1.3 extension. SEAT has
<a =
href=3D"https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-fossati-seat-early-attestat=
ion/" target=3D"_blank" =
data-outlook-id=3D"0000682b-6042-4e85-8053-1c24b9898147">
=
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-fossati-seat-early-attestation/</a>=
.</div>
<div class=3D"ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message skipProofing">41 high =
class CVEs were filed against it:
<a href=3D"https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-intra-handshake-fail/" =
target=3D"_blank" =
data-outlook-id=3D"1314b3b9-9217-4597-904f-2cc2c7183e61">
https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-intra-handshake-fail/</a></div>
<div class=3D"ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message skipProofing">They =
also provided patch to fix. The patch was never applied.</div>
<div class=3D"ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message skipProofing">Anyone =
who talks about CVEs is given "official warning" by chairs.</div>
<div class=3D"ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message skipProofing">Is it in =
scope of your mailing list
<a href=3D"https://listi.jpberlin.de/mailman/listinfo/ietf-discussion" =
target=3D"_blank" =
